{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-loop-note.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 96 recorded why the run-loop observation did not reach the panic, and the behavioural detail the attempt revealed instead.\\n\\nWhat happened. I built a single-replica harness that starts the replica's own event loop and queues the same legal NOOP commit the crash checks use, so that any panic would happen inside the loop's goroutine rather than in a handler call. The exploration reported that the loop survived, and the reason is a timing property of the loop itself: before it serves anything the replica spends about ten seconds in peer-latency measurement (twenty ping rounds with a half-second sleep each), so a started replica does not enter its select loop — and therefore does not accept client connections — for roughly that long. The harness's two-second wait left the commit unprocessed, which is what the output showed.\\n\\nWhat the attempt also showed. A listen failure is silent under a non-verbose logger, because the logger's Fatal prints and exits only when verbose; that is consistent with the reader-side observation from the earlier exploration and with the production launcher's use of a verbose logger.\\n\\nConsequence for the findings. The process-death step of the crash findings (C4 and C11) therefore remains an inference from the run loop having no recover, which both reviews already recorded as a limitation; observing it inside the loop would need a harness that waits out the measurement phase and provides a listener the sandbox permits, or a package-level injection point the implementation does not have. The ten-second measurement phase is now an observed startup property rather than an assumption, and the failure mode of a future attempt is documented so it is not repeated.\\n\\nState. Audit spec version 21; the twelve claim families, the map at version 20, the two capacity-limited items (a review for the pending client-reply artifact, unit-plus-review capacity for the reader observation), the two paused candidates, the configuration premises and the attribution issue on the superseded C1 artifact are all unchanged, and no requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened.\"}"}}
